<h1>What Is a SIP? A Simple Guide for Beginners</h1>
<p>A plain-language guide from Finvestro.</p>
</section>

<main class="wrap"><article class="info" style="margin-top:0"><p>A SIP, or Systematic Investment Plan, is a way to invest a fixed amount in a mutual fund scheme at regular intervals, usually every month. You do not need a large sum to begin. Many schemes allow a SIP from ₹500 a month.</p>
<h2>How does a SIP work?</h2>
<p>On a date you choose, the amount is taken from your bank account and used to buy units of the scheme at that day’s price. When the price is low you get more units, and when it is high you get fewer. Over time this averages out your buying cost. This is often called rupee cost averaging.</p>
<h2>A simple example</h2>
<p>Suppose you invest ₹1,000 every month for 15 years and the investment grows at an assumed 12% a year. You would have invested ₹1,80,000, and the estimated total value would be about ₹4,75,931. This is only an illustration. Real returns can be higher or lower, and they are not guaranteed. You can try your own numbers in our <a href="calculators.html#sip">SIP calculator</a>.</p>
<h2>Why people choose SIPs</h2>
<p>• It builds a regular saving habit.<br>• You can start small and increase the amount later.<br>• You do not have to guess the “right time” to invest.<br>• You can usually pause or stop it when needed.</p>
<h2>Things to keep in mind</h2>
<p>• Mutual funds are subject to market risk, and the value of your investment can go down as well as up.<br>• Choose a scheme that matches your goal and the number of years you can stay invested.<br>• SIPs work best over a long period. Stopping in a market fall can hurt your result.</p>
<h2>How to start</h2>
<p>Complete your KYC, choose a scheme with the help of your distributor, pick a monthly date and set up the bank mandate. If you would like help, <a href="index.html#contact">contact us</a> or <a href="https://wa.me/919166646162?text=Hi%20Finvestro%2C%20I%20read%20your%20blog%20and%20would%20like%20to%20talk." target="_blank" rel="noopener">message us on WhatsApp</a>.</p>
